 "setup": "Rolling-origin backtest over the last 12 months: from each of 10 month-ends (one month apart) we forecast the next 3 months using only the data up to that point, then compare with what customers actually ordered. Units per month. Error = WAPE (absolute error as % of volume); bias = over (+) or under (-) forecasting as % of volume. Overall = all 15 country x product series pooled. Customer-level rows cover the 379 intermittent customer x product series (ordering in fewer than 1 month in 1.32 on average before the first origin). Dirty: the models learn from the spreadsheet view (POs plus leaked enquiries, purchase requests and master data requests, raw customer records) but are scored against the real confirmed POs.",
